-- title:
--   Measure equivalence is strictly below unitary equivalence of bounded operators
-- statement:
--   Let $\equiv_m$ be mutual absolute continuity on Borel probability measures on Cantor space. Let $\equiv_u$ be unitary conjugacy on all bounded operators on the canonical complex separable infinite-dimensional Hilbert space, equipped with the Borel structure of the strong operator topology. Then
--   $$\equiv_m<_B\equiv_u.$$
--   This is Theorem 1.5 of the benchmark-comparisons manuscript, formerly Theorem 1.3 of the measure-equivalence manuscript.
-- source:
--   Ruijun Wang, Comparisons of benchmark equivalence relations, Theorem 1.5 (formerly MeasureEquivalence.tex, Theorem 1.3); supporting declaration OperatorCoding.theorem_13_proved in OperatorStrictSeparation.lean, lines 46–49; local source SHA-256 9bcb1d01d60c8a118ae34b2241b8b63acc853889c608c3ea32265f47e366f38c. Designated upload repository: https://github.com/RayjunWang/Benchmark (no source commit published yet).

